{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-84:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-84:a67e96b54b23ed6b712149eea442830c73341c90e36c0e0f9495a135b6ac55ec","timestamp":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.7w","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-84","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-84","title":"Bob Refs Tabs filter — a Highlights tab switcher","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.7w","updated_at":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"In Bob Mac Capture's Bob Refs panel, ⇧⌘O pressed while Highlights is frontmost (or ⌘T inside the panel) shows a \"Tabs\" filter. It lists every document open in Highlights, matched to its reference note where one exists, with the current tab first and the previous tab pre-selected. ↵ switches to that existing tab without touching the vault or the open log. Bob Mac Capture installs with a stable signing identity, so the Accessibility grant the feature needs survives every `just install`.","design":"plan:202610/highlights_tabs_switcher.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202610/highlights_tabs_switcher.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-84:000002:issue_created:bob-cli-84.1:8acfcba106dd6b9a51e2380e792d4ed8be8b3fc99124b3b182169326397c33b5","timestamp":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.7w","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-84.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-84.1","title":"Stable signing identity and Accessibility status","status":"open","issue_type":"phase","parent_id":"bob-cli-84","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.7w","updated_at":"2026-10-15T21:50:48Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"signing: `just install` signs with a stable self-signed \"Bob Mac Capture Local\" identity when it exists, and otherwise falls back to ad-hoc with a loud warning. `bundle.sh` keeps its ad-hoc default for agent scratch builds. The ad-hoc warning now mentions Accessibility. Settings › References shows \"Highlights tabs: Allowed / Not allowed\" through a small AccessibilityTrust helper. The README documents creating the identity.","design":"","model":"","size":"small","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Epic plan plan:202610/highlights_tabs_switcher.md defines phase signing as one work unit","dependencies":[]}}}
